  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The United States recently experienced a wave of technical outages affecting multiple sectors, including the Federal Aviation Administration, the National Security Agency, and the banking industry. These widespread disruptions prompted significant public and political concern regarding a potential systemic or coordinated cyberattack on American infrastructure. In response to the failures, the White House removed Sean Cairncross from his position as national cyber director, replacing him with Kirsten Davies. Previously, officials including Rubio stated that the country was not under a systemic attack. President Trump recently addressed the situation, explicitly denying claims that the outages were linked or part of a broader, coordinated security breach. Instead, the administration maintains that the series of incidents resulted from separate, isolated technical issues rather than a deliberate, multi-pronged strike against government or private sector digital systems.",
